  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Tuesday)\nIssued at 152 PM CDT WED JUN 3 2026\n\nA large dome of surface high pressure is present across Eastern\nConus today. Some scattered cloud cover is present across the\nsouthwest portions of the area. Otherwise, mostly sunny skies are\nnoted on satellite. Fair and less humid weather is expected to\npersist through the short term forecast (through Friday) as the\nsurface ridge remains the dominant feature. By Thursday, the\nridge center will begin to nudge southeast as the overall ridge\nslowly weakens. Temperatures will be below normal in the short\nterm but will slowly rise each day headed into the weekend.\n\nOnshore flow returns this weekend in the lower levels as the\nsurface ridge continues to weaken and push off into the Western\nAtlantic. Shortwave disturbances will propagate periodically\naround a Deep South and Gulf upper ridge through the extended.\nThis will result in daily diurnally enhanced convection chances\nstarting Saturday.\n\n08",
